      "design": "r0B",
      "good": "The wider definition column produces more readable phrases and shorter rows. Examples also have a little more room than in r0A.",
      "problems": "Several row identifiers visibly break inside words, including Idempotency, consistency and Backpressure. That damages the first column's primary scanning function, despite the reported split count.",
      "cause": "At 95px, the term column provides only 74px of text width, less than the 99px needed by its longest unbreakable word. The extra definition width comes at the expense of intact identifiers."
    },
    {
      "design": "r0C",
      "good": "The wider example column gives examples more natural phrases and makes them easier to read across from the definitions.",
      "problems": "Term identifiers and long definition words visibly split, and definitions become very tall stacks of short lines. Examples frequently end far above the bottom of their rows, weakening the visual balance between the companion columns.",
      "cause": "The 110px term column provides 89px of text width, below the 99px needed, and the 120px definition column provides 99px, below its 108px longest word. Giving 129px to examples leaves too little space for the longer definitions."
    }
